{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]She followed him from Gali[Eb]lee when he had set [Bb]her free
She stood beside the cross [Eb]of him where oth[F]ers feared [Gm7]to be
She watched them lay him in the tomb [Eb]and roll the stone in [Bb]place
And came before the morning light [Eb]to weep for [F]his dear [Bb]face
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The tomb was standing open and the [Eb]stone was rolled away
They [Gm7]have taken away my [Eb]Lord
And [Bb]I don't know where they have put him
[Eb]She turned around and saw a [Gm7]man there in the early grey [Eb]
[Gm7]Thinking he was the gardener, she said
[Eb]Sir, if you have carried him off
Tell me where you have put him
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Jesus [F]said to her, Ma[Eb]ry
She turned to [Bb]him
Rabbo[Eb]ni
[Gm7]I have [F]seen the [Eb]Lord
I have seen the [Bb]Lord
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]Do not hold on to [Eb]me
Go to my broth[Bb]ers and tell them
[F]I am ascend[Eb]ing to my Father and your Father
To my God and your God
